IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 29/6/2026 to 20/10/2026" (a rendering, not the official text): the CORE.
-- Nouns only: DECLARE. No rule is written here, and no constant that belongs to one provision.
-- Every part of the Act imports this module and reads it, never edits it.
-- A part that lacks a type or constructor defines its own under its own provision label
-- (s 240(1)(a) ..., sch 2 para 2 ...) and records it in NEEDS-CORE.md; the lead hoists it at the merge.
--
-- Conventions the whole family follows.
--   Money is a NUMBER, in Singapore dollars.
--   A date is written Date day month year (never year first), from IMPORT daydate.
--   A period is counted only by sfa-periods.l4; no part writes its own date arithmetic.
--   A name that begins "s " or "sch " belongs to the provision it implements; the names below do not,
--   so a part's name can never collide with one of these.
--
-- Membership test: could a witness of ordinary competence testify to the fact,
-- or does answering it need the Act? Only the first kind is here.
-- So a "kind of product" below is what a person would CALL the thing (a share, a bond), never the Act's conclusion
-- (that it is "securities", "capital markets products" or a "debenture"): those are rules, in sfa-definitions-*.l4.

§ `The people and bodies the Act names`

-- The party of a regulative rule, and the word for who a fact is about.
-- The first twelve are people or corporations and carry a name.
-- The last four are bodies of the State or the statutory Council: they appear only as what they mean to the
-- individual in the seat (the encoding has no seat for them), and carry no name.
DECLARE Party IS ONE OF
    Individual HAS `the name of the person` IS A STRING                    -- a natural person: the individual in the seat, or anyone else
    `A corporation` HAS `the name of the corporation` IS A STRING          -- a corporation (s 2(1) "corporation"); the holding company of a group is one
    `A director` HAS `the name of the director` IS A STRING                -- a person in the position of director of a corporation (s 2(1) "director")
    `An officer` HAS `the name of the officer` IS A STRING                 -- an officer of a corporation (s 2(1) "officer")
    `A chief executive officer` HAS `the name of the chief executive officer` IS A STRING   -- s 2(1) "chief executive officer"
    `A substantial shareholder` HAS `the name of the substantial shareholder` IS A STRING   -- s 2(6)
    `A substantial unitholder` HAS `the name of the substantial unitholder` IS A STRING     -- s 2(1) "substantial unitholder"
    `A holder of securities` HAS `the name of the holder` IS A STRING      -- anyone who holds, or has an interest in, securities, derivatives contracts or units
    `An issuer` HAS `the name of the issuer` IS A STRING                   -- the person who issues, or proposes to issue, securities, debentures or units
    `An offeror` HAS `the name of the offeror` IS A STRING                 -- the person who makes an offer of securities, debentures or units
    `An investor` HAS `the name of the investor` IS A STRING               -- the person to whom an offer is made, or who deals
    `A trustee` HAS `the name of the trustee` IS A STRING                  -- a trustee, including the trustee of a trust of units or debentures
    `The Authority`                                                        -- the Monetary Authority of Singapore (s 2(1) "Authority"; carries no name)
    `The Minister`                                                         -- the Minister
    `The Court`                                                            -- the court
    `The Securities Industry Council`                                      -- the body in s 2(1) "Securities Industry Council" (Part 8)

-- A corporation, known by its name.
DECLARE Corporation HAS
    `the name of the corporation` IS A STRING

-- What kind of body something is, for s 2(1) "entity": the Act's "includes" list, and its one closed exclusion.
DECLARE `Kind of entity` IS ONE OF
    `a corporation`
    `an unincorporated association`
    `a partnership`
    `the government of a state`
    `a trust`
    `some other body`

-- The relatives an individual's connected persons are drawn from (s 2(1) "connected person" (a)(i)).
DECLARE `Family relation` IS ONE OF
    `a spouse`
    `a son`
    `an adopted son`
    `a stepson`
    `a daughter`
    `an adopted daughter`
    `a stepdaughter`
    `a father`
    `a stepfather`
    `a mother`
    `a stepmother`
    `a brother`
    `a stepbrother`
    `a sister`
    `a stepsister`
    `some other relation`

§ `The things the Act names: what a person calls them`

-- The thing held, dealt in or offered, as a person would describe it. Whether it is "securities", a "debenture",
-- "capital markets products" or "specified products" is the Act's rule (sfa-definitions-products.l4), not a fact.
DECLARE `Kind of product` IS ONE OF
    `a share`
    `a unit in a business trust`
    `an instrument conferring or representing an ownership interest in a corporation, partnership or limited liability partnership`
    `a bond, note, debenture stock or other debt security`
    `a unit in a collective investment scheme`
    `a derivatives contract on securities or a securities index`
    `a derivatives contract on something else`
    `a spot foreign exchange contract for leveraged foreign exchange trading`
    `a bill of exchange`
    `a certificate of deposit issued by a bank or finance company`
    `a cheque, letter of credit or order for the payment of money`
    `some other product`

-- The classes of investor s 4A(1) names. A person is asked which, if any, applies (the Part 13 exemptions turn on them).
DECLARE `Class of investor` IS ONE OF
    `an accredited investor`
    `an expert investor`
    `an institutional investor`
    `none of the classes in section 4A(1)`

-- The votes attached to the voting shares in ONE class of a corporation's shares, as the register shows them.
-- A corporation with one class has one of these; s 2(5) is asked over a LIST of them.
DECLARE `Class of voting shares` HAS
    `the name of the class` IS A STRING
    `the votes attached to the voting shares in the class that the person has an interest in` IS A NUMBER
    `the total votes attached to all the voting shares in the class, excluding treasury shares` IS A NUMBER

-- A prospectus, as a witness can describe it: who issued it and when the Authority registered it.
-- Its contents and its validity are rules of Part 13, not here.
DECLARE Prospectus HAS
    `the name of the person who issued the prospectus` IS A STRING
    `the date the Authority registered the prospectus` IS A DATE
    `the prospectus relates to debentures` IS A BOOLEAN

§ `The penalty an offence provision states`

-- One shape for every part. Amounts are Singapore dollars, terms are months. A provision that states no fine, or no
-- imprisonment, puts 0 and says so in its own comment; the booleans say whether the text allows both together.
DECLARE Penalty HAS
    `penalty: the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `penalty: the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `penalty: the text allows both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `penalty: the highest further fine for each day the offence continues, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
